        "original_id": "31309b30-f292-5bb4-b38b-4f0848a36382",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy\n- Places: South Africa\n- Products: Ixia, Rhexia, Ixia polystachya, Iridaceae, Ixioideae, Melastomataceae\n\nFacts:\n- Ixia is a genus of cormous plants native to South Africa.\n- Ixia belongs to the Iridaceae family and the Ixioideae subfamily.\n- Rhexia is a plant genus in the Melastomataceae family.\n- Melastomataceae has about 4,500 species in 150 genera.\n- Ixia polystachya is a species in the genus Ixia.\n- Ixia polystachya is also called white-and-yellow-flower cornlily.\n- Ixia polystachya is found on hills and slopes in the northwest and southwest Cape of South Africa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
